.TH HSH 1 "2026" "version 1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- a simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh
.br
.B echo
.RI [ command ]
.B |
.B hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple command interpreter (shell), similar in spirit to
.BR sh (1).
It reads commands, either from an interactive terminal or from
standard input, and executes them.
.PP
When run with standard input attached to a terminal,
.B hsh
displays a prompt,
.RB ( "$ " ),
and waits for a command. When standard input is not a terminal
(for example, when piped from another program), no prompt is
displayed, and commands are read and executed one line at a time
until end-of-file.
.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment variables, one per line.
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell. Any memory allocated by the shell is freed before
exiting.
.SH COMMAND EXECUTION
For any command that is not a builtin,
.B hsh
searches for an executable as follows:
.IP \(bu 4
If the command contains a slash
.RB ( / ),
it is treated as a relative or absolute path and executed directly if
it is accessible and executable.
.IP \(bu 4
Otherwise, the directories listed in the
.B PATH
environment variable are searched, in order, for an executable file
matching the command name.
.PP
Once found, the shell creates a child process with
.BR fork (2)
and runs the program with
.BR execve (2),
passing it the current environment. The parent process waits for the
child to terminate with
.BR wait (2)
and returns the child's exit status.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B hsh
returns the exit status of the last command executed. If a command
is not found, the exit status is set to 127. If a call to
.BR fork (2)
fails, the exit status is 1.
.SH ERRORS
If a command cannot be found or executed, an error is printed to
standard error in the form:
.RS
.I program_name: line_number: command: not found
.RE
.PP
where
.I program_name
is the name the shell was invoked with (its
.IR argv[0] ),
and
.I line_number
is the number of the command line that produced the error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive use:
.RS
.nf
$ ./hsh
$ /bin/ls
hsh main.c shell.c
$ exit
$
.fi
.RE
.PP
Non-interactive use:
.RS
.nf
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
hsh main.c shell.c
.fi
.RE
.SH BUGS
Does not support logical operators
.RB ( "&&" ,
.BR "||" ),
pipes, I/O redirection, comments, or built-ins beyond
.B env
and
.BR exit .
.SH AUTHOR
See the AUTHORS file at the root of the project repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR execve (2),
.BR fork (2),
.BR wait (2)
